From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Wang <jimwan@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sdm-backend: port early renderer callbacks to paint nodes

Weston 15 renderer attach and damage callbacks receive a weston_paint_node
instead of the older surface/buffer arguments. Recover the surface and current
buffer from the paint node before applying the existing GBM-buffer detection.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Jim Wang <jimwan@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 sdm-backend/early-renderer.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sdm-backend/early-renderer.c b/sdm-backend/early-renderer.c
index 6cc1e28..90b0de1 100644
--- a/sdm-backend/early-renderer.c
+++ b/sdm-backend/early-renderer.c
@@ -99,16 +99,17 @@ early_renderer_destroy(struct weston_compositor *ec){
 }
 
 static void
-early_renderer_flush_damage(struct weston_surface *surface)
+early_renderer_flush_damage(struct weston_paint_node *pnode)
 {
 }
 
-
 static void
-early_renderer_attach(struct weston_surface *es, struct weston_buffer *buffer)
+early_renderer_attach(struct weston_paint_node *pnode)
 {
+	struct weston_surface *es = pnode->surface;
+	struct weston_buffer *buffer = es->buffer_ref.buffer;
 	struct wl_shm_buffer *shm_buffer;
 	struct gbm_buffer *gbmbuf;
 
 	weston_log("early renderer attach\n");
 	if (!buffer)
-- 
2.34.1
